// v3.std.anthropic_operations -- per-operation rows for the Anthropic
// service, populating the `Operation` substrate carrier in
// `src/v3/std/services.dag` (PR-α #1246; sharp-raven-604).
//
// SCOPE (T-Ground services.dag PR-β, Phase 1 pilot): row population
// only — single Messages operation. Substrate Manager dispatched
// anthropic first per narrow-scope pilot (parallel to #1195's
// `MethodTemplateContract` Phase 1 row population). The legacy
// authority at `dsl/extdeps/llm/anthropic.dag:168-220` (the
// `service llm.Anthropic { ... operation Messages { ... } }` block)
// remains the v2 emit-pipeline source-of-truth until Phase 2
// retirement (separate dispatch); the row-list here is net-additive
// in PR-β. Phase 1.5 / Phase 2 retirement of the v2 service block
// folds into Pure-Bootstrap-Zero / v2 retirement scope (parallel to
// the LanguageSpec `*_method_templates` deferral pattern landed in
// #1210 + #1213).
//
// HOME (post-#1187 audit lesson): this file lives under `src/v3/std/`
// because v2's `collect_dag_sources` walks `dsl/` recursively (see
// historical pipeline integration tests) — placing this file in
// `dsl/extdeps/...` would re-trigger the cross-tree-import
// regression. The bootstrap-fixture authority
// (`src/v3/std/extdeps_bootstrap_fixtures.dag`) plus
// `BOOTSTRAP_FIXTURE_PATH_KEYS` (`src/v3/compiler/src/bootstrap.rs`)
// resolve mixed-tree fixtures across `STAGED_FILES` and `EXTDEPS_FILES`.
//
// SOURCE OF TRUTH for this row's content:
// `dsl/extdeps/llm/anthropic.dag:180-203` `operation Messages`:
//   - input fields: api_key, model, messages, max_tokens, temperature, system
//   - transport: method=POST, path="/v1/messages"
//
// CALLABLE-EDGE (#1246 + #1266 chain):
//   `Operation.callable: CallableRef { decl: DeclarationRef }` resolves
//   to the top-level callable declaration whose REST realization this
//   row mirrors. Substrate's #1266 landed `fn anthropic_messages` at
//   `src/v3/std/anthropic_messages.dag` for exactly this purpose. The
//   row carries `callable: { decl: anthropic_messages }`. Display
//   names + per-operation identity derive from `callable.decl` via
//   `DeclarationRef` resolution; per `services.dag:107-114`,
//   `Operation` deliberately does NOT carry a parallel `name: String`
//   field that could drift from the callable.
//
// EXPLICIT DEFERRAL §1 — INPUT-FIELDS POPULATION
// (parser-grammar gap; Substrate-tracked Phase 1.5+ slice):
//
// The v2 source declares 6 input fields (api_key, model, messages,
// max_tokens, temperature, system), but `Operation.inputs:
// Map<String, InputField>` per `services.dag:124` cannot be
// populated inline because v3's grammar does not currently support
// nested string-keyed `Map<String, X>` literals in record-field-value
// positions. Even an empty literal `{}` doesn't satisfy the
// structural type — it parses as an empty record, not an empty Map,
// and the row fails the `Operation.inputs` shape check
// (`ResolveError: data anthropic_operations field <list element>
// does not match the declared structural type`).
//
// Audit at HEAD: every existing `Map<String, X>` data item lives at
// top-level (`algebra.dag:460`, `types.dag:65/79/114/133`,
// `node.dag:207`, etc.); zero precedent for nested construction.
// Cross-manager request routed from R2 Grounding Manager (#1133
// inbox 4353126932); Substrate has queued the parser slice as
// Phase 1.5+ work (#1130 comment 4353153545).
//
// Pilot impact: the Messages row (POST /v1/messages) has zero
// `ParamToken`s, so the `ParamToken.name` → `inputs` boundary check
// is vacuous regardless. The deferred input-field-keys assertion is
// load-bearing only for future ParamToken-bearing rows (GitHub
// provider operations, etc.). For now the entire pilot row is
// deferred (the empty-list scaffolding lands; populated row
// re-arms once the grammar extension lands).
//
// Parallel to: Go `chars` tokenizer deferral (#1196 hot-fix).
//
// EXPLICIT DEFERRAL §2 — v2 PARAMETER DEFAULTS
// (`InputField.default` carrier; Substrate-tracked Phase 1.5+ slice;
// distinct gap from §1):
//
// v2's `max_tokens: Int = 4096` carries a parameter default not
// represented in PR-β rows. PR-α `InputField {}` is empty terminal;
// the `InputField.default` carrier is queued as a Phase 1.5+
// Substrate slice (Substrate disposition #1130 comment 4352585286).
// Until that slice lands, PR-β rows are honest about the v2
// service-block input shape **minus the defaults**. The default is
// preserved in legacy v2 source until the carrier lands — no silent
// drop.
//
// Parallel to: `*_method_templates` PB-Zero deferral (#1210 / #1213),
// `string_contains` Modeling-level classification deferral, Rust
// higher-order Phase 1.5 deferral.
//
// **Distinct gaps, distinct dispositions** (per #1133 inbox
// 4353159066): §1 is a parser-grammar question; §2 is an
// `InputField` schema question. Each has its own cross-manager
// citation and its own dissolution trigger.

module v3.std.anthropic_operations

import std.types { HttpMethod, POST }
import v3.std.services {
  Operation,
  RestEndpointBinding,
  InputField,
  CallableRef
}
import std.effects {
  PathTemplate,
  UrlPathToken,
  LiteralToken
}
import v3.std.anthropic_messages { anthropic_messages }


// **PHASE 1 PILOT ROW DEFERRED — parser-grammar gap deeper than
// expected (per #1133 inbox 4353126932 routing call):**
//   The Messages row construction `{ callable: { decl: anthropic_messages },
//   inputs: <empty>, endpoint: { ... } }` cannot typecheck against
//   `Operation` today because `inputs: Map<String, InputField>` has no
//   inline literal form that satisfies the structural type. Empty
//   record `{}` parses but fails the `Map<String, InputField>` shape
//   check (`ResolveError: field <list element> does not match the
//   declared structural type`). The cross-manager request to Substrate
//   for the parser-grammar extension (nested `Map<String, X>` literals
//   as record-field-values, including empty `Map`) is queued; PR-β
//   Phase 1 lands the **substrate-fixture-authority extension + test
//   machinery** as net-additive scaffolding so the Messages row drops
//   in mechanically once the grammar lands. Same hot-fix discipline as
//   #1196's empty Go method-template-contracts list.
//
// Test-side: the lockstep checks for this row are wired but vacuously
// pass on the empty list. Phase 1.5+ row-fill grows them to the
// pilot-row checks named in the test header.
data anthropic_operations: List<Operation> = []
